WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.534
-I'm always happy to see you. You look gorgeous as always.

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.067
-Oh, you're so sweet. -Stunning.

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:08.234
Backstage, I've got to say, I got to see --

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:10.100
I want to call them "the kids." -Yes.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.734
-The twins. They're still kids, right?

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:13.634
-Of course they're kids. They're 11 years old.

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:16.434
They can't drink for another 10 years.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:17.701
-Yeah, that's true. Yeah, you're right.

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:19.334
Roc and Roe.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.234
They're actually -- There they are on the side of the stage.

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:24.000
-Hey, Roc and Roe. -They are so cute...

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.667
[ Cheers and applause ] -Yes.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:26.968
Roc -- he said to me --

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:28.467
I go, "What do you think of the beard?"

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:31.033
He goes, "I like it. I like that with the suit."

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:33.467
And Roe was like -- I go, "What do you think?"

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.834
And she goes, "It's not bad."

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:37.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.934
So,I'll take that as a win. -It's a compliment.

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:42.267
-Is it, though? -Well, I'm hoping so.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.000
-Yeah, they're very sweet.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.567
I've known them since they were baby babies.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.701
-They were baby babies. -They're so cute.

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:50.934
Millie Bobby Brown was on our show a couple weeks ago,

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:53.267
and she was telling us that you guys

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.868
actually are friends

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.434
and, like, you're a mentor to her.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.267
She also teased that there may be

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:00.434
a musical collaboration in the works.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:01.734
-Did she, now?

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.367
-Just saying -- -Maybe it's not just musical.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.267
I don't know. I can't say what it is.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.667
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.567
-Wow. Alright. That's a good scoop.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.501
I'll take that. I won't press anymore, yeah.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:15.634
-Yeah, no, no, no. It's fun tings.

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:18.934
-Millie did an impression of what it's like

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.534
to have dinner at Mariah Carey's house.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:21.868
-Oh, dear. Okay. -Let's take a look at this.

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:23.968
-She's good at impressions. -I go over to her house,

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.400
and I'll be, like, eating dinner,

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.868
and she'll come around and she'll be like --

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:28.734
[ Vocalizing ] I'll be like...

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:31.033
-No, for real?! -No, it's a real thing.

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:33.133
It's not like -- People are like --

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:34.234
No, no, no, no, no.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:35.601
She does it when we're eating Chinese food.

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.400
-Wait! What?! -It's wild.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.968
-She's not lying.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:40.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.534
She's not lying.

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:44.234
-So you'll just be having Chinese food

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:45.834
and you just go into the high note?

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.734
-I can't define which type of food it is.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.501
We're not allowed to do that anymore.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.300
I don't know what type of food it was.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.100
-Yes, your right. -We were having morsels.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.801
-But you will break into -- -No, not really --

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.601
I mean, sort of. I mean, it depends on the moment.

00:01:57.601 --> 00:02:00.267
Right now I'm just like --- Two days of vocal rest,

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.868
ready to get back and get moving

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:03.434
with some other projects happening.

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.434
-By the way, you had a giant summer, by the way,

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:09.334
with "Big Energy (Remix)" with DJ Khaled and Latto.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:12.367
That was a giant. -That was -- That did --

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:13.801
-Congratulations. -Thank you.

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:16.400
-You were also inducted into the Songwriters Hall of Fame.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.033
-Thank you very much.

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.467
One of my fellow collaborators right there.

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:21.767
James James.

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:24.467
-What did that night mean to you?

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:27.033
-I'll just give this little bit of info.

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:30.501
So, there's this -- We've had some memes.

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:33.334
And one of the more --

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:36.400
one of the ones I see quite a bit is me going,

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.200
"As a songwriter, as a songwriter, as a songwriter."

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.701
So, I'm sitting there -- Because most people

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:45.400
don't give me the credit that I feel

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.501
after writing 18 number-one singles...

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:50.534
[ cheers and applause ] Well, I would say 19.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:53.400
-I mean, come on. -I would say 19.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.801
Is that the slow clap beginning? -No, I was gonna stand up.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:57.868
I was ready to stand up for you.

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:01.267
-Enh-enh. -Respect. I love it.

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:03.100
-Please and thank you. But, no, no.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.434
The truth is, people will ask about, oh --

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:07.968
Now they're saying, "Tell us about your process

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:09.334
and this and that."

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.667
It's not about awards really. That night meant a lot.

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:14.033
Because it was -- it was validating.

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:17.534
But it was also, like, as a woman starting out so young

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:21.167
in this industry, most people are given songs

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.968
and given, like, "Here's how you're going to do this

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.467
and this is what you should do."

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:27.067
That was the one thing I said in my contract when I was really --

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:28.968
had to have, like -- my mom had to be there.

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:31.000
I was too young to even sign the thing on my own.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.734
And I was like, "The one thing I will insist on..."

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:34.167
It was -- [Bleep]

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:35.968
But, anyway, the one thing I insisted on

00:03:35.968 --> 00:03:38.067
is, "You cannot make me do other people's songs."

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.300
Like, that's the one thing.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.234
Like, I at least had to have that input.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:43.501
That's where I talk to Millie about stuff.

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:44.767
That's kind of what she meant,

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.734
I think, about a mentor and a guide.

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:48.901
Like, don't give it away if you don't have to.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.601
-Yeah, good. Good for you.

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:52.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:53.934
Trailblazing.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:56.767
I do want to talk about this thing that was just announced.

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.734
You kind of -- Christmas came early

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:00.133
to all of us when you announced

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:01.934
"Merry Christmas to All" Christmas concerts

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:03.400
at Madison Square Garden.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.334
You just added a second show, by the way.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:10.868
What is -- What can we expect from this?

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:13.434
-Expect the unexpected. I don't know, darling.

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:15.167
-Really? -We're putting a really --

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:17.634
Well, we went on sale with the presale, right?

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:21.400
And that happened like -- That was a quick moment I heard.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.767
-Oh, definitely.

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:24.300
-I don't follow these, like, statistics.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.434
Time is irrelevant to me. I don't acknowledge it.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:28.267
-Okay. -That's why even in my book,

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.934
this book, there's no page numbers.

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:31.601
Somebody had to point that out to me.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.968
So I was like, "Oh, yeah." Well, 'cause I don't care.

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:37.067
'Cause it's all the same. It should all just be the same.

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:40.501
-Yeah, okay. -Why? Anyway.

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:43.968
No. So I realized that the best thing I could do is just talk

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:46.934
to the fans, be with the fans, sing to the fans, with them.

00:04:46.934 --> 00:04:49.634
And it's an inclusive experience. It's so fun.

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:51.334
The last time we did Madison Square Garden

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:53.133
was pre-COVID, 2019.

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:56.701
The most fun I ever had doing a show because it snows.

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:59.133
I don't want to give it away. I don't want to give it away.

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:01.701
It's festive, and we may or may not be

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:05.267
seeing it on a network/ streaming service, as well.

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:08.067
-Whoa! -Coming to you.

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:09.501
-Dropping all the nice scoops tonight.

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:10.734
Thank you for that.

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:12.267
-Well, I don't know if it's a scoop or not.

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:13.601
They better scoop me the information

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:15.701
so I can get it all scooped and smoothed.

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:18.234
That's kind of what's perfect about getting into the book.

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:21.467
It's all about love, and it's about the love of Christmas

00:05:21.467 --> 00:05:23.868
and the love of the song and the love that's in a song.

00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:26.167
-And bringing people together really is the thing.

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:29.834
'Cause what I really said in this is that it's not just about

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:31.968
"'Cause here name is Mariah and she's little Mariah.

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:34.434
La la la. I'm so Christmasy." Whatever.

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:35.767
It's not that.

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:38.133
It's that this is for anyone who's ever felt othered,

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:40.567
who's ever felt different than other people,

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:43.067
who's ever felt ostracized, you know what I mean?

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:44.868
Maybe you don't feel like you're --

00:05:44.868 --> 00:05:46.868
Not to throw out the vocab words,

00:05:46.868 --> 00:05:48.567
because they always throw it at me.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:50.734
[ Cheers and applause ] No, but it really is.

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:52.300
And so, at the end of the day,

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.501
it's not a magical prince that comes and saves her day.

00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:55.901
It's the music.

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:58.334
But she gets through her own struggles and her own stuff.

00:05:58.334 --> 00:06:00.934
And ultimately, in my opinion, this is --

00:06:00.934 --> 00:06:03.267
It's the adventures of little Mariah.

00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:06.133
She represents all people, little boys, little girls,

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:10.934
little whoever, everybody that needs that inspiration.

00:06:10.934 --> 00:06:13.334
And it's fun and festive! -She's so cute.

00:06:13.334 --> 00:06:15.167
-And her hair's a little bit unkempt.

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:16.434
-Yeah, she's cute.

00:06:16.434 --> 00:06:18.300
-She's not perfect. She doesn't get a makeover.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.701
Can I ask you maybe to do a little reading from the book?

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:22.734
Would that be okay? -I mean, if you'd like.

00:06:22.734 --> 00:06:24.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.434 --> 00:06:27.934
I wasn't given a -- Oh, look at this.

00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:30.300
This is gonna be my new favorite cup at home.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.734
-Oh, my gosh. I would love that. Please.

00:06:32.734 --> 00:06:34.868
-I'm not gonna tell you who else's cup is there.

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:36.367
-Don't tell me, please.

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:37.934
Don't ruin the dream for me, will you?

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:40.334
-Oh, stop that. Stop that. -Darling, darling.

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:41.634
-Darling.

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:43.234
-Darling, where would you like to begin?

00:06:43.234 --> 00:06:47.267
-Okay. So, we'll start here.

00:06:47.267 --> 00:06:49.767
"In the middle of the rundown dwelling

00:06:49.767 --> 00:06:54.300
was an unsteady flight of wooden stairs with rickety rails.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.601
Little Mariah had to watch where she stepped

00:06:56.601 --> 00:06:59.567
and had to beware of pesky little nails,

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:02.567
popping up out of nowhere, snaggin' her stockings,

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.200
prickling her pinky toe,

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.934
then snickering when they were done.

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:09.667
Pesky snickering nails in the stairs

00:07:09.667 --> 00:07:13.901
with rickety rails really was no fun.

00:07:13.901 --> 00:07:18.100
One brilliant spot inside the dank shaky shack

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:20.667
was an old golden-brown upright piano,

00:07:20.667 --> 00:07:22.834
elegant, solid, and bright,

00:07:22.834 --> 00:07:25.834
whose black and white keys held all the hopes

00:07:25.834 --> 00:07:29.501
and possibilities of music, joy, and light.

00:07:29.501 --> 00:07:32.200
Sitting on the bench humming a marvelous melody

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:35.501
written in her mind was the one place in the world

00:07:35.501 --> 00:07:38.801
Little Mariah felt she belonged and was alright."

00:07:38.801 --> 00:07:40.200
Then enters --

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.834
This is just me editorializing, but it's true.

00:07:42.834 --> 00:07:45.167
Mike the Bird, who is one of our villains.

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:46.767
He's a two-faced parrot.

00:07:46.767 --> 00:07:49.801
And he's really nice when he's around certain people.

00:07:49.801 --> 00:07:51.634
But when he's mad, whatever.

00:07:51.634 --> 00:07:55.334
So when he's with Little Mariah by herself, he goes like this.

00:07:55.334 --> 00:07:57.133
This is real -- This part --

00:07:57.133 --> 00:07:59.033
It's a fairy tale. This is a fairy tale.

00:07:59.033 --> 00:08:01.400
But I still have a scar from this parrot.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.000
That's serious.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.934
-My gosh. You actually do. -I really do. Okay.

00:08:04.934 --> 00:08:06.601
So, he goes...

00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:08.767
[Gravelly voice] "Mariah!

00:08:08.767 --> 00:08:10.734
[ Laughter ]

00:08:10.734 --> 00:08:13.701
Time to brush the hair!"

00:08:13.701 --> 00:08:16.100
-Ohh! Wow.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.567
[ Laughs ]

00:08:17.567 --> 00:08:20.567
That's real! That's how you read a book.

00:08:20.567 --> 00:08:23.734
Come on. Mariah Carey. We love you.

00:08:23.734 --> 00:08:26.534
"The Christmas Princess" is available now.

00:08:26.534 --> 00:08:29.968
We'll be right back with Marcus Mumford. Stick around.

